  "term": "transient global amnesia",
  "definition": "Transient global amnesia is a sudden, temporary episode of memory loss that is usually brief and typically happens as a single event. It mainly affects memory for recent events and reduces the ability to form new memories, without being linked to a neurologic disorder.",
